{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Suspected defect\nA source-path audit at code revision d49466b5e960 suggests that one completion operation may combine code evidence read from the immutable tree selected by `--ref` with prefetch, deterministic checks, or later signing inputs rooted at the live checkout. This is a hypothesis from control-flow inspection, not a demonstrated failure. It MUST be verified experimentally before any production change.\n\nThe public contract is that checks which judge the implementation are based on the code revision supplied by `--ref`. Comparisons against live state can be valid for drift detection, ancestry, optimistic concurrency, or publication safety, but live checkout content must not become verdict evidence for a `--ref`-targeted run.\n\n## Mandatory reproduction before remediation\n1. Build a disposable Git fixture with revisions A and B whose source, referencing commit evidence, and a prefetched file deliberately disagree. Keep the live checkout at B and invoke the real completion path with `--ref A`.\n2. Instrument or spy on every code-root/ref input used by context assembly, completion prefetch, deterministic commit/file checks, verifier tools, drift checks, and completion-signature material. Record the resolved OID and classify each read as verdict evidence, ticket-state evidence, or an intentional live-state comparison.\n3. Prove whether all verdict-bearing code reads resolve to A. If they do, record the falsification and close this bug without a speculative refactor. If any verdict-bearing read resolves to B, preserve the failing experiment as the regression test before changing code.\n\n## Remediation constraints if reproduced\n- Thread one explicit pinned-code handle/OID through every verdict-bearing path; do not let a generic `repo_root` silently select live code.\n- Keep intentional live comparisons explicit and one-way: they may reject/retry stale work, but may not contribute evidence that makes a criterion pass or fail.\n- Bind `verified_at_sha` and the completion signature to the same A selected by `--ref`.\n- Cover a moving branch name as well as a concrete SHA, resolving the name once at operation start.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A deterministic divergent-A/B experiment proves or falsifies the suspected mixed-root behavior through the real completion orchestration path. (Held-out oracle `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch_pinned_root_831f.py` drives the REAL `gate_source.gate_read_root(attested A)` + `assemble_prefetch(repo_root=live B)` path; Phase-1 runtime experiment reproduced the same via the real orchestration. PROVED (not falsified): prefetch read B.)\n- [x] The evidence records the resolved OID and purpose of every code read used by prefetch, deterministic checks, agent file tools, drift comparison, and signing. (RCA comment classifies each: prefetch working-tree reads -> now the pinned snapshot A (was live B, the leak); reconcile citations -> A via `cfg.repo_path` at `gate_ops.py:290`; agent read_file/search_files -> A via `use_code_root(handle.path)`/`cfg.repo_path`; `referencing_commit_diffs` -> immutable-by-SHA object read (not live checkout evidence); drift guard -> one-way live comparison, not verdict evidence; signing -> `verified_at_sha`=`handle.sha`=A.)\n- [x] If reproduced, a regression test fails before the fix when live=B and `--ref=A`, then passes only when every verdict-bearing check uses A. (Same held-out test: verified RED at buggy HEAD (prefetch carried `LIVE_B_CONTENT`), GREEN after the re-root fix; mutation-checked -- re-seeding the exact defect on both `_read_body` and `_discover_test_globs` re-roots turns it RED.)\n- [x] Intentional live-state comparisons are named and tested to fail closed or retry without becoming verdict evidence. (The transition-close drift/stale guard is the sole intentional live comparison: it compares live HEAD/ref against the pinned `verified_at_sha` to reject/retry stale work and never feeds verdict evidence -- covered by `tests/unit/test_attested_close_guard.py`. The fix does not touch it; audit confirmed it stays one-way.)\n- [x] The emitted `verified_at_sha` and signed completion manifest equal A. (`gate_source.annotate_result` binds `result[\"verified_at_sha\"] = handle.sha` (=A) and marks the run `signable` only when attested + pinned SHA -- `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py:232`; provenance covered by `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance.py`. Already correct; audit-confirmed, unchanged by this fix.)\n- [x] If the experiment falsifies the hypothesis, no production behavior is changed and the ticket closes with the falsifying evidence. (Inapplicable branch: the experiment CONFIRMED the hypothesis rather than falsifying it, so the \"no production change\" path was not taken; the localized re-root fix landed instead. Recorded for completeness.)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787941437344216001,"uuid":"93f58bce-5dd3-444f-8b04-68829255e7f7"}